A||N||4||G-Nasty||Strange noise  on fast take-off||||1||
Z||000000||G-Nasty||01-17-2001||10:41 PM||||I am getting a popping / clunking noise coming from the rear axles on my 87 GT w/ 5 speed. I have had 4 fieros and the other ones never made this sound. It only makes the sound when I take off quickly and put a "load" on the car. Any ideas? This car has 108K miles on it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-17-2001||10:46 PM||||Check the two large bolts that hold the strut to the knuckle.  It's possible they came loose.  <P>This just happened to me with an '87 GT I just sold......The right rear squirmed when I took a hard corner.  Come to find out the strut was loose. <P>Other options are a bad engine mount, bad tranny mounts or a bad engine dogbone.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||01-18-2001||12:04 AM||||Couldn't that also be the inboard CV joints going bad?<P>One way to find out if it's a mount.. take the decklid off and have a friend drive around while you watch the engine through the back window.  Or you could sit in the trunk, but I'd recommend a helmet for that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||
Z||000003||Alex2004||01-18-2001||10:42 PM||||I had that problem before, and we had to replace the tranny. mine is an auto. It made a loud noise from the axels like that, and kinda shook when you accelerated real quick.  We took it to some shop to see if they could fix it, I can't remember what it was exactly, but it was real expensive to fix, so we got a tranny out of another Fiero from a member of the Fiero Club of Oklahoma for $75 as long as we gave him the old one.  So, i would have someone check it out first, and if they can't fix it.  I'd just get another tranny.  Hope that helps some, i'll ask dad tomorrow what it was exactly ok.<P>Alex...<p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||G-Nasty||01-19-2001||12:04 AM||||I have one of those "ultimate" dogbones and my other mounts keep the engine from shaking by hand unlike my other gt engine. I have a 5 speed and it really sounds like CV joints because its a crackling sound that only appears when i get on the gas from a start. Thanx for all the info dudes-I may keep my other car just in case it is tranny gears...||||reg||1
